# probe-18 notexists_correlate_cost
# GAP: FILTER NOT EXISTS lowers its inner triples (rewrite.rs:175-196) but the anti-join is
#   generic and is NOT known to share the batched-correlated machinery (PR-4b/4c/4d) built for
#   OPTIONAL. q017/q053 are the corpus tail members of exactly this shape. This probe stresses
#   the OTHER direction (a FACT driver with a FACT existence check) to see whether the negated
#   FACT_PAYMENT side is materialized once (hash anti-join) or re-scanned per outer order
#   (correlated) — the difference between seconds and DNF on a ~fact-sized driver.
# MECHANISM that SHOULD fire: a single-materialize hash anti-join, or budgeted correlation.
# PREDICTED: if per-row correlated, scan_table on FACT_PAYMENT fires many times / huge span
#   count -> likely timeout; if hash, two bounded scans. Telemetry (scan_table n, span count)
#   discriminates.
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT ?oid
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?o a edw:Order ; edw:orderId ?oid .
        FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?p a edw:Payment ; edw:order ?o . } }
LIMIT 5000
